# smbclient — real-world examples

## List shares on a server (anonymous)

```sh
smbclient -L mediaserver -U%
```

## List shares as a named user

```sh
smbclient -L mediaserver -U david
```

## Connect to a share interactively

```sh
smbclient //mediaserver/media -U david
```

## Pull a file without an interactive session

```sh
smbclient //mediaserver/media -U david -c 'get movie.mkv'
```

## Mount-free recursive download of a folder

```sh
smbclient //homelab/backups -U david -c 'recurse ON; prompt OFF; mget *'
```

## Flag reference

| Flag         | What it does                       |
| ------------ | ---------------------------------- |
| -L host      | list shares on host                |
| -U user      | authenticate as user               |
| -U%          | anonymous / no password            |
| -c 'cmds'    | run commands non-interactively     |
| -m SMB3      | force a protocol version           |

> On Tumbleweed, install with `sudo zypper install samba-client`.
